.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Claude Code local overrides (settings.json itself is shareable; .local is not)
.claude/settings.local.json

# ─── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json

# ─── skin-mcp project outputs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Projects normally live under --project-root (default ~/.skinmcp), outside the
# repo. These patterns catch a stray run started with `--project-root .`.
#
# All anchored with a leading slash: `src/skinmcp/runtimes/` and
# `src/skinmcp/prompts/` are SOURCE and must stay committed. An unanchored
# `runtimes/` would silently delete the R Dockerfile, renv.lock and every vetted
# script from the repo.
/projects/
/objects/
/figures/
/tables/
/notebooks/
/returns/
/logs/
/models/
proj_*/

# ─── Data ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Including tests/golden/golden_mouse_skin.h5ad: 12.5 MB, and deterministically
# regenerable with `python tests/golden/make_golden.py` (seed=0). conftest.py
# rebuilds it automatically if it is missing, so CI and a fresh clone both work.
*.h5ad
*.h5
*.loom
*.mtx
*.rds
*.zarr/
*.pkl
*.pickle

# SQLite project memory, including the WAL sidecars that WAL mode creates
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Exported artifacts
*_bundle.zip
methods_draft.md
memory_export.md
memory_export.json
/report.md
/report.html

# ─── R runtime ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# renv.lock and the Dockerfile ARE committed; the restored library is not.
renv/library/
renv/local/
renv/staging/
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
.Rproj.user/

# ─── Reference material ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 234 MB of embedded notebook outputs. Keep it local; the extracted patterns it
# contributed are documented in NOTICE and reproduced in style/panels.py.
reference/macrophages_resident_recruited.ipynb

# ─── Jupyter ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Opening the reference notebook or an exported analysis.ipynb creates these.
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*-checkpoint.ipynb

# ─── Scratch ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
scratch/
tmp/
.tmp/

# ─── Third-party source checkouts ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# mem0 is a declared dependency (`pip install -e .[memory]`, PyPI: mem0ai), not
# vendored source. A local clone here is only for reading or patching upstream;
# it must not be committed, and nothing in skinmcp imports from it by path.
mem0-main/

# Milo writes one figure per parameter hash, so every test run mints a new
# filename instead of overwriting. 234 of them had accumulated (35 MB), 84
# already committed. Nothing reads them -- tests assert on the data behind the
# figures, not the files -- so they are output, not fixtures.
tests/golden/figures/**/milo_beeswarm_da_*
tests/golden/figures/**/milo_nhood_graph_da_*
